---
title: Vieux Carré
servings: 1
tags: [cocktail, whiskey]
source: Classic cocktail, number 46 on Drinks International's 2026 bestselling classics; method written for this repository
---

In a #mixing cup{}(with ice), pour @rye whiskey{0.75%fl_oz}, @cognac{0.75%fl_oz}, @sweet vermouth{0.75%fl_oz} and @Bénédictine{1%tsp}. Add @Peychaud's bitters{2%dashes} and @Angostura bitters{2%dashes}. Stir well, and strain into a #rocks glass{}(with a large cube). Garnish with a @lemon peel{1%twist} or a @cocktail cherry{1}.

> Created by Walter Bergeron at the Hotel Monteleone, New Orleans, in 1938.
